Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: a render pass needs an attachment, so say side-effects-only is unsupported

  case SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_SHADER_WITH_ONLY_SIDE_EFFECTS:
      return true; // WebGPU render passes work with no color attachments.

The comment is wrong. WebGPU requires a render pass to carry at least one
non-null color attachment or a depth-stencil attachment; a pass with neither is
invalid, and reports exactly that:

  No attachment was specified.

Godot already has the fallback for APIs that cannot rasterize on side effects
alone. cluster_builder_rd.cpp branches on this very capability: true takes
framebuffer_format_create_empty(), false creates a real color attachment and
selects the USE_ATTACHMENT shader variant that patch 0015 added. So the correct
fix is to answer the capability question honestly and let Godot's own branch do
the work, rather than inventing a dummy-attachment path inside the driver.

Cost is one unused color attachment on the cluster-build pass. The alternative
was a pass that never executed.

Measured on a Tesla P40 through Chrome/WebGPU, Chariot on Forward+:

  attachmentless render-pass errors   2 -> 0
  GPUValidationError                 14 -> 6   (with 0024)

diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
--- a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
@@ -9284,7 +9284,14 @@
 		case SUPPORTS_HALF_FLOAT:
 			return false; // WebGPU shader-f16 extension not reliably available; avoid f16 in generated SPIR-V.
 		case SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_SHADER_WITH_ONLY_SIDE_EFFECTS:
-			return true; // WebGPU render passes work with no color attachments.
+			// WebGPU requires a render pass to have at least one color attachment or
+			// a depth-stencil attachment; a pass with neither is a validation error
+			// ("No attachment was specified."). Reporting true made the cluster builder
+			// take framebuffer_format_create_empty() and fail every frame. Reporting
+			// false selects Godot's existing USE_ATTACHMENT path, which binds a
+			// throwaway color target -- the cost of one unused attachment, in exchange
+			// for the pass actually executing.
+			return false;
 		case SUPPORTS_IMAGE_ATOMIC_32_BIT:
 			return false; // WebGPU has no image atomics support.
 		case SUPPORTS_MULTIVIEW:
